Aerie-Purpose: Remove the onboarding page's "download uBlock Origin filter lists" toggle, its strings and its pref, since the bundled uBlock Origin is gone.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: components/helium_onboarding (the onboarding page asset unpacked from deps.ini: HeliumServices.svelte, lib/browser/prefs.ts, lib/chrome-send-polyfill.ts, helium_onboarding_strings.grdp)
Aerie-Kind: hook

The asset is not in Helium's patches: the build unpacks it into the tree before any patch applies
(helium-chromium/deps.ini [onboarding]), and this patch applies to that unpacked source. The strings
header and strings.ts are generated from the .grdp, so removing the two messages removes
s.services.ublockTitle and ublockDesc, and the page no longer lists the toggle. The matching
settings toggle and pref were removed with the dropped ublock-helium-services patch.

--- a/components/helium_onboarding/src/pages/HeliumServices.svelte
+++ b/components/helium_onboarding/src/pages/HeliumServices.svelte
@@ -26,8 +26,2 @@
         {
-            title: s.services.ublockTitle,
-            desc: s.services.ublockDesc,
-            prefName: "services.ublock_assets",
-            available: !platform.is.android,
-        },
-        {
             title: platform.is.linux
--- a/components/helium_onboarding/src/lib/browser/prefs.ts
+++ b/components/helium_onboarding/src/lib/browser/prefs.ts
@@ -12,3 +12,2 @@
     'services.browser_updates': boolean,
-    'services.ublock_assets': boolean,
 };
--- a/components/helium_onboarding/src/lib/chrome-send-polyfill.ts
+++ b/components/helium_onboarding/src/lib/chrome-send-polyfill.ts
@@ -30,3 +30,2 @@
     'services.browser_updates': true,
-    'services.ublock_assets': true,
 };
--- a/components/helium_onboarding/helium_onboarding_strings.grdp
+++ b/components/helium_onboarding/helium_onboarding_strings.grdp
@@ -73,8 +73,2 @@
 </message>
-<message name="IDS_HELIUM_ONBOARDING_SERVICES_UBLOCK_TITLE" desc="Title of the toggle for downloading uBlock Origin filter lists.">
-  Allow downloading filter lists for uBlock Origin
-</message>
-<message name="IDS_HELIUM_ONBOARDING_SERVICES_UBLOCK_DESC" desc="Description of the toggle for downloading uBlock Origin filter lists.">
-  Helium will fetch fresh filter lists for uBlock Origin. All requests to lists are proxied to protect your privacy. When disabled, default filter lists will be loaded from local storage, which are only updated along with Helium. Optional filter lists will be requested without proxying.
